1a77188bc","file":"preprints/The-complete-Crouzeix-theorem-September-23-2026/build/main.tex","line":116,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"30db59b1044ab87a9a0ab6deee032c49929b2b8a6f3191e7a79d731ecb8858e5","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-complete-Crouzeix-theorem-September-23-2026/build/main.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:3d4dbc5e87d34763684367d3add07d0087f8538943dbbff78a7ad121a77188bc","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-complete-Crouzeix-theorem-September-23-2026/build/main.tex#L116"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:structural}\nFor every admissible $\\Omega$, every finite $n\\ge1$, every\n$A\\in M_n(\\C)$ with $W(A)\\subset\\Omega$, and the interior conformal\ncoordinate $f$ above, the problem \\eqref{eq:minimum} is strictly feasible\nand has an attained minimum $1\\le\\kappa^2\\le4$. If $H$ is a minimizing\nmetric, then\n\\[\n S=H^{1/2},\\qquad A'=SAS^{-1},\\qquad D=Sf(A)S^{-1}=f(A')\n\\]\nsatisfy\n\\[\n D^*D\\preceq I,\\qquad \\rho(D)<1,\n \\qquad \\|S\\|\\|S^{-1}\\|=\\kappa\\le2.\n\\]"}
